  "result": {
    "summary": "All four fix-round findings are addressed in the T-1282 worktree. I did not run the test suite, and I did not open the test files or the docs beyond the fallback lines. (1) `_choice` is back to returning `ambiguous` for the catch-all case, and no `test_result` fallback branch remains. The ambiguous list, counts and reduction stats do not depend on `cache_mode`. (2) `FALLBACK_REASONS` is `frozenset(('ambiguous',))`, which is the only reason `_choice` assigns when no named rule matched. It has no source_type names, and the docs state this at line 14. (3) The `scout_packet` change is reverted: `spawn.py` has no diff against goal/T-0991 in that area. (4) `_context_mode` now returns `(mode, cache_mode, invalid_config)`, and `_shadow_route` passes `effective_mode`, `cache_mode` and `invalid_config` to `route()` explicitly. `cache_mode` is validated once in `_context_mode`. `route()` no longer validates it, and `cfg` carries no hidden flag. Shadow mode only records adjusted levels, and the adjusted level is applied only when both `cache_mode` and the effective mode are active. That is a sound trust boundary, and the change introduces no privilege escalation. Low-risk note: `provider` defaults to `codex` in `packet` and `claude` in `review_packet`, which is consistent with the executor and reviewer roles.",
